# Use case: send sensor readings to the cloud and get commands back.
#
# The module joins Wi-Fi, connects to a public MQTT broker, listens on a command topic and
# publishes a reading. The broker sends the message back, which proves the whole round trip
# (Wi-Fi, DNS, internet, broker) works. Swap the broker and topics for your own when ready.
#
# You need: a NORA-W36 EVK and the Wi-Fi name and password in the environment:
#   $env:UCX_WIFI_SSID = "MyNetwork"; $env:UCX_WIFI_PASS = "MyPassword"
#   .\ucxapp --script examples/use-cases/sensor-to-cloud.ucx
# Watch it from a PC or phone with any MQTT client: broker.emqx.io:1883, topic ucxapp/evk/#
wifi.connect ${UCX_WIFI_SSID} ${UCX_WIFI_PASS}
mqtt.connect broker.emqx.io 1883
expect connected to broker.emqx.io
mqtt.subscribe ucxapp/evk/#
mqtt.publish ucxapp/evk/temperature {"celsius":21.5}
mqtt.read 10
expect ucxapp/evk/temperature: \{"celsius":21.5\}
mqtt.disconnect
